# EXPECTED root-lane counts for the NEXT lane run — COMMITTED BEFORE IT RUNS.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (D0A-R21-07). Two consecutive lane runs had a correct figure and a
# WRONG explanation: R19-06 (a "+2" that named an internal test leg as a second #[test]) and
# R20-07 (a "+1" that named a test which already existed). The second happened while claiming
# the first had made attribution "checkable".
#
# NO DATES OR COMMIT HASHES ARE WRITTEN IN THIS FILE (D0A-R22-02). The first version recorded
# both by hand and BOTH WERE WRONG: it dated the predictions 2026-08-29 when the commits are
# 2026-08-30 and the result is 2026-09-01, and it labelled them "committed at <hash>" using
# the TREE THEY WERE DERIVED FROM rather than the commit that introduced them. A hand-copied
# provenance in the one file whose entire claim is *git establishes the ordering* can only be
# redundant or false. It was false. Use:
#
#   git log --format='%h %ad %s' --date=iso -- .githooks/runtime-test-count-baseline.expected
#   git log --format='%h %ad %s' --date=iso -- .githooks/runtime-test-count-baseline.root
#
# TARGET_TREE below names the tree the derivation was computed against — a DIFFERENT thing
# from the commit that introduces this file, and conflating them is what produced the error.
#
# WHAT CONSUMES IT: NOTHING. The ordering is a CONVENTION followed by hand.
#
# `scripts/lane-run.sh` consumed it for exactly one run (run 12) and was then REVERTED —
# D0A-R23 returned 8×P1 against it, including that it had dropped five safety checks
# `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md` performs. A mechanism with eight open P1s that omits
# helper-digest, free-space, forced-freshness, stale-session and PAM before/after checks is
# weaker than a convention a human follows WITH them.
#
# So this file is DOCUMENTATION, NOT PROOF, and says so again rather than quietly reverting to
# the claim R22-01 falsified. What run 12 proved is banked and survives: its artifact binds
# expectation commit c16c3e9 to tree 0330b46, and that remains checkable.
#
# PROTOCOL
#   1. Derive the expectation from the unprivileged pair and the root-gating of each change.
#   2. Commit THIS FILE ALONE, with the derivation in the message.
#   3. Run the lane.
#   4. Commit the measured pair in `.githooks/runtime-test-count-baseline.root`, SEPARATELY.
#   5. A mismatch is a RESULT. Record which side was wrong; do not adjust the derivation
#      until it agrees.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPERSEDED — LANE RUN 11, first expectation. NEVER MEASURED.
#
#   EXPECTED_EXECUTED=174  EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5   TARGET_TREE=d6fb698
#
# Derived from an unprivileged 154/25; the R21-03 and R21-05 tests then moved the tree to
# 156/25 before run 11 happened. Drift is the normal case and the protocol answers it by
# RE-DERIVING in a separate commit, not by adjusting — amending would have been tidier and
# would have made the file indistinguishable from a claim written after the fact.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LANE RUN 13 — THE FULL-HYGIENE RUN. TARGET_TREE: this commit.
#
# WHY THIS RUN EXISTS: D0A-R24-01. Run 12 went through `scripts/lane-run.sh`, which omitted
# helper-digest, forced-freshness, stale-session and PAM before/after — so the current root
# evidence is split across two runs covering different dimensions (run 11 hygiene, run 12
# counts+ordering). This run replaces both with one record covering everything.
#
# DERIVATION — checkable, not asserted:
#   run 12 measured           EXECUTED=176 SKIPPED=5   (at unprivileged 156/25)
#   unprivileged is now       EXECUTED=157 SKIPPED=25  (+1 since run 12)
#   the +1 is `reached_the_anchor_rejects_an_unrelated_permission_error` (D0A-R24-04), and
#   it is NOT root-gated — grepped for a geteuid check, a SKIP branch and a
#   bwrap_available guard across its body: ZERO hits. It is a pure predicate test with no
#   process spawn, so it executes at root exactly as it does unprivileged.
#   therefore 176 + 1 = 177, and NO skip changes.
#
# The five root skips are unchanged: b1_daemon_binary (needs --features
# insecure-test-seams), live_logind_query (standing DEFER), and three that skip BECAUSE the
# run is privileged (an_unreadable_login_defs, a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused,
# pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier).
#
# THE ORDERING IS BACK TO CONVENTION (D0A-R22-01, reopened). Nothing reads this file before
# the run. `git log` on this file and on the .root file is the only evidence of ordering, and
# it is evidence only if this commit contains THIS FILE ALONE.
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=177
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LANE RUN 11 — MEASURED 176/5, matching. TARGET_TREE=298d4db
#
#   EXPECTED_EXECUTED=176  EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
#
# DERIVATION, written so it can be checked rather than believed:
#   run 10 measured           EXECUTED=173 SKIPPED=5   (at unprivileged 153/25)
#   unprivileged at 298d4db   EXECUTED=156 SKIPPED=25  (+3 since run 10)
#   the +3, each VERIFIED not root-gated by grep (no geteuid check, no SKIP branch, no
#   bwrap_available guard), so each executes at root as well:
#     1. service::tests::a_gate_denied_action_sends_no_preview
#     2. action::tests::preview_renders_the_bound_schema_version
#     3. service::tests::an_oversized_preview_is_denied_before_the_action_is_stored
#   therefore 173 + 3 = 176, no skip change.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LANE RUN 12 — the first run through `scripts/lane-run.sh`. TARGET_TREE: this commit.
#
# DERIVATION — the prediction is that NOTHING MOVES, which is a real prediction and not a
# default, because it rests on a checkable claim:
#
#   run 11 measured              EXECUTED=176 SKIPPED=5   (at unprivileged 156/25)
#   unprivileged is STILL        EXECUTED=156 SKIPPED=25
#   changed since run 11's tree  runtime/src/service.rs ONLY (+18/-4)
#   new `#[test]` since then     ZERO  (`git diff 298d4db..HEAD -- runtime/ | grep -c '^+    #\[test\]'`)
#
#   The commit touching runtime/ since run 11 is af46083, carrying BOTH R22-07 (the
#   no-preview regression's
#   read no longer turns every error into EOF) and R22-08 (the module doc's flow
#   renumbered) — ONE commit, not two (D0A-R23-11). Neither fix adds or removes a test
#   and neither is root-gated, so the root pair is unchanged.
#
# THE ONE THING THAT COULD MOVE IT, named so a mismatch has a first suspect: R22-07 changed
# `a_gate_denied_action_sends_no_preview` to PANIC on a read error where it previously
# returned 0. That test runs at root. If a privileged socketpair read behaves differently
# there — EINTR under load, say — the test would newly FAIL rather than silently pass, and
# EXECUTED would hold while the extractor's rc went non-zero. That is the failure this change
# was made to expose, so seeing it would be the fix working, not the prediction being wrong.
#
# Everything else in this range is documentation, the corpus (classes 47 correction and 48),
# and the lane runner itself with its own shell suite — none of which is a Rust test.
#   (run 12: EXPECTED_EXECUTED=176 EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5 — measured, matched)
